Dear all,

I am trying to perform a moderated mediation model in lavaan, but I seem
to have trouble getting the interaction factor in the model.

My model code is this:

model3.2 <- ' # direct effect

             SecurityCC ~
c1*AAI_2forcedCC

           # mediator

             Sens_centr ~
a1*AAI_2forcedCC

             SecurityCC ~
b1*Sens_centr

           # Moderator

             SecurityCC ~
c2*NE_centr

             SecurityCC ~
b2*Sens_centr:NE_centr

             SecurityCC ~
c3*AAI_2forcedCC:NE_centr

         '

fit <- sem(model3.2, data = data_sens_temp, missing =
"pairwise", ordered = c("SecurityCC"),
link="probit")

summary(fit)

SecurityCC and AAI_2forcedCC are factor variables (binary), Sens_centr
and NE_centr are continuous variables.

When I run this model, I get an error saying that some variables have no
values (only missings). When I look in the specifications, I can see that this
is the case for the interaction variables ‘Sens_centr:NE_centr’ and ‘AAI_2forcedCC:NE_centr’.
I don’t understand why this is not working, because I thought the ‘:’ is used
to create an interaction term. I do prefer to have the interaction made in the model, because I intend to run the same model in a set of imputed datasets. Can anyone give me some advice on this?

Thanks so much in advance!

Marije

